in that pileup.

254
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.400
Which means Death
could be coming for us.

255
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.300
Yeah, like, what if

256
00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.800
we're all getting that 'Different Strokes'
curse or something?

257
00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.500
I think you're all
are certifiable.

258
00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.600
I can't believe I've been listening
to this crap.

259
00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.300
Let's go.
Let's go, Tim.

260
00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.100
Mrs Carpenter, please.

261
00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:57.400
Kimberly!

262
00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.600
Oh baby!

263
00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.100
- Are you okay?
- I'm so sorry.

264
00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.700
Shh, shh.

265
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.100
You can all go now.
Thank you for your patience.

266
00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.600
Could I ask you something?

267
00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:32.000
Anything.

268
00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.700
Did Mum ever have any...

269
00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.200
I don't know,
weird feelings about anything?

270
00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.900
What do you mean?

271
00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.900
Like visions or premonitions.

272
00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.200
Sweetie, are you sure
you're okay?

273
00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:52.900
Dad, I know
this sounds crazy,

274
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.200
but I'm really scared
for the others.

275
00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.900
I don't know,
I have this really bad feeling.

276
00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.500
What?

277
00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.100
It's not over yet.

278
00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.200
Jesus Christ!

279
00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:31.100
Shit!

280
00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:00.600
Hey, Evan, it's Tawny.

281
00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:02.500
Sorry I haven't called.

282
00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:05.200
Hey, listen, I heard
about your lottery win.

283
00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:07.800
Let's hook up.
Call me.

284
00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:10.200
Yeah.

285
00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.900
Hi, Evan, it's Nikki.

286
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.100
We met at Tucker's party
last year?

287
00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:16.600
I know it's been awhile,
but I've been thinking about you.

288
00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:19.300
I just wanted to say
congratulations.

289
00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.300
So give me a call.

290
00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.500
555-0123. Bye.

291
00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:26.800
You little bastard.

292
00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:28.500
Shit.

293
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:36.000
Come on.
Come on.

294
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Fuck. Fuck.

295
00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:56.600
Come on!

296
00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:58.200
Come on.

297
00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:05.700
Fuck!

298
00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:07.200
Jesus!

299
00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:15.900
Oh!

300
00:23:22.600 --> 00:23:24.400
Hey, this is Evan.
Leave a message.

301
00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:26.900
If you're looking for Rick,
I don't know where he is,

302
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.600
and I don't know
when he's coming back. Thanks.

303
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:33.500
Evan, call me when you
get in, you lucky fuck!

304
00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:02.900
Come on! Come on!
Come on!

305
00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:04.500
Aah!

306
00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:35.200
Jesus!

307
00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:41.300
Come on.

308
00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:50.500
Aah!

309
00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:55.000
Shit, I'm lucky.

310
00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:59.000
Aah!

311
00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.900
Jesus Christ!

312
00:26:26.300 --> 00:26:28.200
No, Mother,

313
00:26:28.300 --> 00:26:30.800
just turn on any station.

314
00:26:30.900 --> 00:26:34.000
Well, I don't know how you missed it,
it's been on all day.

315
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:36.500
Yes, Mother,
Channel 4 is fine.

316
00:26:36.600 --> 00:26:39.600
Okay... here it is!
I got to go, okay?

317
00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:41.500
I got to go!

318
00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:44.200
To recap our top story,

319
00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:47.700
Route 23 was backed up
for almost nine hours today.

320
00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:50.900
A record-breaking pileup
killed an estimated 18 people.

321
00:26:50.800 --> 00:26:53.700
Emergency crews spent hours
sifting through the wreckage

322
00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:56.800
hoping to recover any survivors
from this tragic collision.

323
00:26:57.000 --> 00:26:59.800
So far police are refusing
to release the names of the victims

324
00:26:59.800 --> 00:27:01.400
until the families
are notified.

325
00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:03.400
The camera
of a highway patrol car

326
00:27:03.400 --> 00:27:05.200
managed to catch
this shocking footage.

327
00:27:05.300 --> 00:27:07.200
- A semi comes...
- Oh my God.

328
00:27:07.300 --> 00:27:09.100
And smashes
into a red SUV.

329
00:27:09.200 --> 00:27:12.600
- The driver of the SUV...
- No, um...

330
00:27:12.700 --> 00:27:14.100
leave it.

331
00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:15.500
...may have
saved her life.

332
00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:17.400
He pulled her back
at the last second

333
00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:19.400
just as the semi ploughed
into the vehicle.

334
00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:21.100
The passengers inside
the SUV...

335
00:27:21.300 --> 00:27:24.000
Oh, oh, oh! You guys see that?!
Shit, I was there, baby!

336
00:27:24.100 --> 00:27:27.900
In other news, a freak accident took
the life of a lotto winner.

337
00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.700
- Friends say Evan Lewis...
- Hey, shh.

338
00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:33.500
Was on top of the world after
recently winning $250,000.

339
00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:36.000
But in tragic turn of events,
Lewis died today

340
00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:38.600
while trying to escape a fire
in his apartment.

341
00:27:38.700 --> 00:27:40.300
He managed to make it out
of the building,

342
00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:42.500
but somehow the ladder
on the fire escape

343
00:27:42.600 --> 00:27:44.400
slipped and impaled him.

344
00:27:44.500 --> 00:27:46.900
Investigators believe Lewis
died instantly.

345
00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:56.700
Come in.

346
00:27:58.500 --> 00:27:59.900
Hey, buddy.

347
00:28:01.300 --> 00:28:04.100
I want you to take this
so you can get some sleep.

348
00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:09.000
And then tomorrow it's off to the dentist,
which I know you love.

349
00:28:10.600 --> 00:28:12.400
Now, get some rest.

350
00:28:16.700 --> 00:28:19.200
- Mum.
- Yeah?

351
00:28:19.300 --> 00:28:21.300
You think those guys
were BSing us today?

352
00:28:21.300 --> 00:28:23.000
Yeah.

353
00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:25.400
Some people just need
some rewiring, that's all.

354
00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:28.200
Lights out.

355
00:30:21.800 --> 00:30:23.800
At the request
of the patient,

356
00:30:23.900 --> 00:30:25.800
you'll relinquish
any sharp objects

357
00:30:25.900 --> 00:30:28.100
such as: 'nail files,
pencils, pens,

358
00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:31.000
safety pins, bobby pins,
your necklace,

359
00:30:31.100 --> 00:30:33.600
matches, lighters,
belts, belt buckles,

360
00:30:33.700 --> 00:30:36.600
earrings, hair clips,
glasses, shoelaces,

361
00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:39.500
paper clips, watches, money clip,
pocket knives,

362
00:30:39.700 --> 00:30:42.200
food, drinks, keys,
cell phone... '

363
00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:44.400
You have a cell phone
on you?

364
00:30:44.500 --> 00:30:47.300
'... poisons, pills,
medications.'

365
00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:49.800
Great. And let me see
your nails.

366
00:30:49.900 --> 00:30:52.400
Good. Then I think
we're all done.

367
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:54.300
Wait.

368
00:30:54.400 --> 00:30:56.200
Is she dangerous
or something?

369
00:30:56.300 --> 00:30:58.200
No, honey,
she expects you are.

370
00:31:00.700 --> 00:31:03.700
No, no, no.

371
00:31:03.800 --> 00:31:06.900
Get him off me.
Get him off me!

372
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:16.500
How long are they gonna keep
her locked up like this?

373
00:31:16.600 --> 00:31:19.000
Depends on her, I guess.
She's voluntary.

374
00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:48.500
- Clear Rivers?
- Don't come any closer.

375
00:31:56.400 --> 00:31:59.700
They told me you had something to do
with the crash on Route 23.

376
00:31:59.900 --> 00:32:02.700
Look, I don't know how
to explain it,

377
00:32:02.700 --> 00:32:05.800
but I saw the pileup
before it happened.

378
00:32:07.400 --> 00:32:09.400
And I saved some people.

379
00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:11.700
And now you think Death
is after you.

380
00:32:13.400 --> 00:32:15.400
Nice work.

381
00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:18.600
Maybe if you're real lucky,
you'll wind up in here with me.

382
00:32:20.100 --> 00:32:21.700
Anything else?

383
00:32:21.700 --> 00:32:24.000
One of the people died
in a freak accident last night.

384
00:32:24.100 --> 00:32:26.100
What if the other people
are in danger, too?

385
00:32:26.200 --> 00:32:28.500
If you put them on the list,
they're already dead.

386
00:32:28.600 --> 00:32:30.800
List? What list?

387
00:32:30.800 --> 00:32:32.900
Death's list.

388
00:32:35.300 --> 00:32:37.400
The survivors of Flight 180

389
00:32:37.600 --> 00:32:39.800
died in the exact order

390
00:32:39.900 --> 00:32:42.500
they were originally meant
to die in the plane crash.

391
00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:45.600
That was Death's original design.

392
00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:48.500
The list.

393
00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:50.900
I was supposed to die
in that crash with my friends.

394
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:52.600
So you're telling me
that I'm next?

395
00:32:52.600 --> 00:32:54.600
You said someone else died
last night.

396
00:32:54.700 --> 00:32:56.700
That means someone must
have intervened.

397
00:32:56.800 --> 00:33:00.800
Officer Burke pulled me away
from the crash that killed my friends.

398
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:02.800
Congratulations.

399
00:33:02.900 --> 00:33:05.400
You'll be the last to go.

400
00:33:05.500 --> 00:33:07.900
But don't worry,
once the others are dead,

401
00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:09.600
it'll come back for you.

402
00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:12.700
It always does.

403
00:33:14.100 --> 00:33:15.700
This doesn't make sense.

404
00:33:15.700 --> 00:33:19.900
You said that you die in
the order you're originally meant to.

405
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:23.600
But my friends died last
in my premonition, not first.

406
00:33:23.700 --> 00:33:25.600
Wait.

407
00:33:26.600 --> 00:33:28.800
Died last?

408
00:33:30.900 --> 00:33:32.700
Backwards.

409
00:33:32.700 --> 00:33:34.700
Are you sure?

410
00:33:36.400 --> 00:33:38.200
In my premonition

411
00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:40.200
that Nora woman
and her kid died.

412
00:33:40.300 --> 00:33:43.200
Then Evan,
then me and my friends.

413
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:48.100
Why is this even
happening to me?

414
00:33:52.400 --> 00:33:54.700
That's what Alex used
to ask himself.

415
00:33:56.400 --> 00:33:58.600
So, what am I
supposed to do?

416
00:33:58.700 --> 00:34:00.500
Clear.

417
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.800
Watch out for the signs.

418
00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:05.600
What?

419
00:34:07.900 --> 00:34:10.800
Have you ever seen anything
creepy or ominous?

420
00:34:10.900 --> 00:34:13.500
An in-your-face irony
kind of thing?

421
00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:18.000
The songs on the radio.

422
00:34:18.100 --> 00:34:20.900
Yeah, the guy in the beer truck,
everything on the road.

423
00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:23.100
Well, don't ignore it.

424
00:34:23.200 --> 00:34:26.700
Recognising those signs usually means
the difference between life and death.

425
00:34:26.900 --> 00:34:29.300
You got to help me.

426
00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:30.900
I don't have
to do anything.

427
00:34:30.900 --> 00:34:32.500
But you beat it.

428
00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:34.300
Take a look around.

429
00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:36.200
What did I beat, Kimberly?

430
00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:41.700
If you were smart, you'd save yourself
and just forget about the others.

431
00:34:41.700 --> 00:34:44.100
How can you say that?
You have a responsibility.

432
00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:46.300
My friends are dead.

433
00:34:46.400 --> 00:34:48.200
That's how I can say that.

434
00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:53.300
This is what happened to Alex
when I was responsible for him.

435
00:34:54.300 --> 00:34:56.200
Get out.

436
00:34:56.300 --> 00:34:58.600
Before you hurt me or yourself.

437
00:35:02.300 --> 00:35:05.000
- Alright, you know what?
- What?

438
00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:06.400
I think you're a coward.

439
00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:08.200
You hide out in here
because you're

440
00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:11.200
too damn bitter and selfish
to help any other person.

441
00:35:11.400 --> 00:35:13.200
In my opinion,
you're already dead.

442
00:35:49.600 --> 00:35:51.600
I tried calling you
last night,

443
00:35:51.600 --> 00:35:53.500
but your father said
you were sleeping.

444
00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:55.300
- Evan Lewis is dead.
- Yeah.

445
00:35:55.500 --> 00:35:58.600
I've been getting calls all morning from
everyone who was on the on-ramp.

446
00:35:58.600 --> 00:36:00.600
We're meeting tonight
at my apartment.

447
00:36:00.700 --> 00:36:03.800
Wait, so...
you believe all this Death stuff?

448
00:36:05.100 --> 00:36:07.600
Well, at first,
no, I didn't.

449
00:36:07.600 --> 00:36:09.500
Until last year
when I was dispatched

450
00:36:09.700 --> 00:36:11.900
to clean up one
of the Flight 180 survivors.

451
00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:13.700
Clean up, I don't...

452
00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:20.300
- Did you see that?
- See what?

453
00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:22.800
- Pigeons.
- Pigeons?

454
00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:24.700
- It's a sign.
- A sign of what?

455
00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:26.500
If Clear's right
about the order,

456
00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:29.600
then Nora and Tim are going
to be attacked by pigeons.

457
00:36:29.700 --> 00:36:31.200
I'm not following you.

458
00:36:31.200 --> 00:36:32.800
They're next
on Death's list.

459
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.400
If we don't find them,
they're going to die.

460
00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:22.900
The doctor's ready
for you, now.

461
00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:24.800
If he gives me the gas

462
00:37:24.900 --> 00:37:26.900
and I wake up
with my pants unbuttoned...

463
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:30.300
- we ain't paying.
- Tim.

464
00:37:37.500 --> 00:37:41.300
There you are.
What happened to you yesterday, Tim?

465
00:37:41.400 --> 00:37:42.100
We missed you in here.

466
00:37:42.200 --> 00:37:44.600
We got hung up by that accident on
Route 23.

467
00:37:44.700 --> 00:37:47.200
Good Lord.
How lucky that you're okay.

468
00:37:48.900 --> 00:37:50.900
Your mum says you've been
having some pain lately.

469
00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.100
Not really.

470
00:38:17.300 --> 00:38:19.200
I'm disappointed, Tim.

471
00:38:19.300 --> 00:38:20.600
Does your mum know
you've been smoking?

472
00:38:20.600 --> 00:38:23.700
Uh-huh.
Ow.

473
00:38:23.800 --> 00:38:25.800
Yeah, that one's going
to have to be filled.

474
00:38:27.100 --> 00:38:28.900
Damn those pigeons.

475
00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:32.200
How many times am I going to have to
replace those goddamn windows?

476
00:38:34.600 --> 00:38:37.300
We can't do it, boss,
we can't do it!

477
00:38:37.400 --> 00:38:39.900
This will only sting for a moment.

478
00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:42.100
Open big.

479
00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:43.700
Little bit wider.

480
00:38:43.800 --> 00:38:45.600
Wider.

481
00:38:45.700 --> 00:38:48.000
Okay.

482
00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:51.200
Oh God.

483
00:38:51.300 --> 00:38:53.000
How do they
expect me to...

484
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.500
Would you rather just have
the laughing gas?

485
00:38:55.700 --> 00:38:57.800
- Yeah.
- Okay.

486
00:38:57.900 --> 00:38:59.700
Jean, I'm going
to need you in here.

487
00:39:02.200 --> 00:39:04.300
You'll have to speak up,
there's too much noise.

488
00:39:06.300 --> 00:39:09.100
What?!
I can't hear you!

489
00:39:09.200 --> 00:39:11.200
Excuse me, what?!

490
00:39:12.500 --> 00:39:15.100
Yes, the sixth at 2:00 P.M.

491
00:39:15.200 --> 00:39:17.800
Jean! Let me
get this started.

492
00:39:19.800 --> 00:39:21.500
Tim, you'll be awake,
a little groggy,

493
00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:23.600
but you're not going
to be able to move much.

494
00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:50.100
Okay, great, thanks.
Alright, turn around.

495
00:39:50.200 --> 00:39:53.300
The cleaning lady said they're at
the Ellis Medical Complex off of 14th.

496
00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:59.700
God damn it anyway.

497
00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:08.800
- Okay, I got it.
- I can't find a box!

498
00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:12.500
Not again. Careful.

499
00:40:52.100 --> 00:40:53.600
There we go.

500
00:41:02.700 --> 00:41:04.600
Jean,
how's Tim doing in there?

501
00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:11.200
What did he say
about your tooth?

502
00:41:11.100 --> 00:41:13.300
- Did he say...
- I can't remember.

503
00:41:13.400 --> 00:41:15.000
- Nora!
- The pigeons!

504
00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:17.300
What? Pigeons?

505
00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:21.000
Hey, whoa, whoa!
Kid, kid!

506
00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:24.600
- No-oo!
- Tim!

507
00:41:24.600 --> 00:41:25.800
Look out!

508
00:41:27.500 --> 00:41:29.800
- Stay back, stay back!
- No! Please, no!

509
00:41:47.400 --> 00:41:49.600
Nora's not coming.
She won't leave her son.

510
00:41:49.700 --> 00:41:53.500
- No, but she's next...
- Right now I don't think she cares.

511
00:42:11.700 --> 00:42:13.800
This is really
happening again, isn't it?

512
00:42:16.100 --> 00:42:17.900
I hoped we'd get there

513
00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:19.900
and they'd be fine,

514
00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.200
and Clear Rivers
was just full of shit,

515
00:42:22.300 --> 00:42:25.900
and Evan Lewis' death
was just some freak accident.

516
00:42:27.700 --> 00:42:29.800
But we're all going to die,
aren't we?

517
00:42:34.100 --> 00:42:36.000
I'm so scared.

518
00:42:37.300 --> 00:42:39.700
I know you didn't ask
for any of this...

519
00:42:40.900 --> 00:42:43.400
but I don't think you have it
in you to quit either.

520
00:42:51.400 --> 00:42:53.100
A second one just died.

521
00:42:53.200 --> 00:42:54.900
A 15-year-old kid.

522
00:42:57.000 --> 00:42:59.000
I hope you're ready for this.

523
00:43:10.100 --> 00:43:11.500
It's this way.

524
00:43:13.900 --> 00:43:16.200
How is this guy going
to help us anyway?

525
00:43:16.300 --> 00:43:18.600
He seemed to know
a hell of a lot more

526
00:43:18.700 --> 00:43:20.600
about Death
than he ever told us.

527
00:43:24.500 --> 00:43:26.400
Shouldn't we knock first?

528
00:43:26.500 --> 00:43:28.700
He probably already knows
we're coming.

529
00:44:14.100 --> 00:44:16.000
Hello, Clear.

530
00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:23.400
I've been expecting you.

531
00:44:23.600 --> 00:44:25.400
Oh my God.

532
00:44:26.900 --> 00:44:29.500
- That's Evan Lewis.
- Come to pick my brain?

533
00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:32.600
Just a simple question and we'll leave you
alone with your new friend.

534
00:44:34.200 --> 00:44:36.100
Dead...

535
00:44:36.100 --> 00:44:38.800
yet still fresh.

536
00:44:40.300 --> 00:44:42.200
Look, we drove
a long way to get here,

537
00:44:42.300 --> 00:44:44.300
so if you happen to know
how to stop Death,

538
00:44:44.400 --> 00:44:46.000
it would be really great
if you told us.

539
00:44:47.100 --> 00:44:48.600
You can't cheat Death.

540
00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:51.300
- There are no escapes.
- Bullshit.

541
00:44:51.400 --> 00:44:54.200
You told me Death
has a distinct design.

542
00:44:54.300 --> 00:44:57.400
But Alex and I cheated Death,
not once but dozens of times.

543
00:44:57.400 --> 00:44:59.800
The design is flawed,
it can be beaten.

544
00:44:59.900 --> 00:45:02.500
Such fire in you now.

545
00:45:02.500 --> 00:45:05.000
People are always
most alive

546
00:45:05.100 --> 00:45:06.700
just before they die.

547
00:45:06.800 --> 00:45:08.500
Don't you think?

548
00:45:24.700 --> 00:45:25.900
Look, please...

549
00:45:32.100 --> 00:45:35.200
if you know of anything
that could help us,

550
00:45:35.300 --> 00:45:37.200
what harm could it do?

551
00:45:38.300 --> 00:45:41.600
Only new life
can defeat Death.

552
00:45:41.600 --> 00:45:43.700
What the hell
does that mean?

553
00:45:45.600 --> 00:45:48.000
Some people say there's a balance
to everything.

554
00:45:49.000 --> 00:45:50.700
For every life
there's a death,

555
00:45:50.800 --> 00:45:53.000
and for every death
there is a life.

556
00:45:53.100 --> 00:45:55.700
But the introduction of life
that was not meant to be,

557
00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:58.100
that can
invalidate the list,

558
00:45:58.100 --> 00:46:01.300
force Death
to start anew.

559
00:46:08.900 --> 00:46:11.300
You have to follow
the signs...

560
00:46:11.400 --> 00:46:13.100
Kimberly.

561
00:46:15.300 --> 00:46:17.200
How do you know my name?

562
00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:32.800
- Whoa!
- Wait a second.

563
00:46:32.900 --> 00:46:35.800
'New life defeats death'?
'Follow the signs'?

564
00:46:35.900 --> 00:46:37.700
Where did you
find that guy?

565
00:46:37.800 --> 00:46:39.400
I thought he was supposed
to help us,

566
00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:40.900
not freak us out.

567
00:46:45.900 --> 00:46:47.500
What the fuck
are you thinking?!

568
00:46:49.400 --> 00:46:52.600
I'm thinking suck on my junk,
bee-atch.

569
00:46:52.700 --> 00:46:54.400
Little punk.

570
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:07.700
What is it?

571
00:47:07.800 --> 00:47:10.100
What did you see?

572
00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:25.100
You have to tell us,
what did you see?

573
00:47:25.100 --> 00:47:27.200
Kimberly, look at me!
You have to tell us.

574
00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:29.300
What did you see?!

575
00:47:32.400 --> 00:47:34.100
I was driving a white van.

576
00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:36.400
I don't know,
I must have lost control,

577
00:47:36.500 --> 00:47:38.200
because I crashed
into a lake.

578
00:47:38.300 --> 00:47:40.400
- And I drowned.
- You were there?

579
00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:43.300
I can practically taste
the water in my mouth.

580
00:47:46.300 --> 00:47:48.000
Wait, remember, the on-ramp?

581
00:47:48.100 --> 00:47:50.700
There was a pregnant woman
in a white delivery van.

582
00:47:50.700 --> 00:47:53.900
He said only new life
can defeat death.

583
00:47:55.400 --> 00:47:56.900
If she gives birth
to a baby

584
00:47:56.900 --> 00:47:58.800
that would've died
in that car crash...

585
00:47:58.900 --> 00:48:01.400
a brand new soul that was never part
of Death's design...

586
00:48:01.500 --> 00:48:03.000
It throws the whole list
out of whack

587
00:48:03.100 --> 00:48:05.200
and we start over
with a clean slate.

588
00:48:05.300 --> 00:48:08.200
- It seems like a reach, don't you think?
- What else could it mean?

589
00:48:08.300 --> 00:48:10.200
We have to find
the pregnant lady's number.

590
00:48:10.300 --> 00:48:11.700
I don't have it.
She never came to the station.

591
00:48:11.700 --> 00:48:15.700
We have to warn her about the lake
so she can stay alive to have the baby.

592
00:48:15.800 --> 00:48:18.800
- That'll be an easy conversation to have.
- How are we gonna find her?

593
00:48:18.900 --> 00:48:20.400
There could be thousands
of white vans in the state.

594
00:48:20.500 --> 00:48:21.700
Hey!

595
00:48:22.700 --> 00:48:24.500
I'm a cop, remember?

596
00:48:27.800 --> 00:48:29.300
Wait, that's it.

597
00:48:32.200 --> 00:48:33.900
Got it.

598
00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:38.300
With the plate number
I can put out an APB.

599
00:48:38.300 --> 00:48:40.300
Here we go.

600
00:48:40.400 --> 00:48:42.200
The vehicle
is a delivery van

601
00:48:42.300 --> 00:48:44.600
registered to Marcus
and Isabella Hudson.

602
00:48:45.800 --> 00:48:47.900
We should pick them up
pretty quickly.

603
00:48:47.900 --> 00:48:49.700
Come on, let's get
to the meeting.

604
00:49:03.800 --> 00:49:05.500
Hey, hold the door!

605
00:49:06.900 --> 00:49:08.800
Hey, let go of my shoe!

606
00:49:08.900 --> 00:49:10.600
Give me my shoe!

607
00:49:16.300 --> 00:49:19.200
I wrote to management two weeks ago
about these friggin' bumpers.

608
00:49:21.100 --> 00:49:23.200
Is that dogshit, dude?

609
00:49:26.300 --> 00:49:27.900
Eww.

610
00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:35.000
Oh, you got something
on your...

611
00:49:38.100 --> 00:49:41.100
It's still there, bro'.
Here, I can get it for you.

612
00:49:42.200 --> 00:49:44.000
No, it's alright.

613
00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:48.000
I'll do it
if you want me to do it.

614
00:49:51.300 --> 00:49:53.000
Just let... I'll...
Let me do it.

615
00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:56.700
What?

616
00:49:57.900 --> 00:49:59.700
Hey, man,
how you doing?

617
00:49:59.600 --> 00:50:01.800
Listen, any word
on that white van yet?

618
00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:05.400
Okay, keep checking.

619
00:50:15.100 --> 00:50:16.900
Does anybody have a Valium?

620
00:50:16.900 --> 00:50:18.800
Oh, yeah.

621
00:50:18.800 --> 00:50:20.400
Here.

622
00:50:20.600 --> 00:50:22.900
You're just going to want to take
half of that.

623
00:50:22.900 --> 00:50:24.400
Keep 'em coming.

624
00:50:27.100 --> 00:50:28.700
If what you're saying is true,

625
00:50:28.800 --> 00:50:30.300
that means I'm next.

626
00:50:30.300 --> 00:50:32.700
This is crazy, people, come on.

627
00:50:32.800 --> 00:50:34.800
First Death
is stalking us,

628
00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:37.200
and now premonitions?
What?

629
00:50:37.300 --> 00:50:38.900
You're not next, Nora.

630
00:50:39.100 --> 00:50:42.200
Nobody has to be next.
That's the point.

631
00:50:42.200 --> 00:50:45.200
We need to help each other
in order to get through this.

632
00:50:45.400 --> 00:50:46.900
This cannot be happening.

633
00:50:46.900 --> 00:50:48.600
See, because my career
is at a peak

634
00:50:48.700 --> 00:50:50.600
and I finally met
a quality guy.

635
00:50:50.800 --> 00:50:52.300
I just bought a house.

636
00:50:52.400 --> 00:50:54.400
Maybe if you shut the fuck up,
you'll live.

637
00:50:55.600 --> 00:50:57.500
Like I'm going
to take advice from you.

638
00:50:57.700 --> 00:51:00.300
Okay, look,
if you know what to look for,

639
00:51:00.300 --> 00:51:01.800
you have a fighting chance.

640
00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:05.300
If I call and say,
I don't know... subway...

641
00:51:05.300 --> 00:51:07.500
Get to a high-rise fast.

642
00:51:09.500 --> 00:51:12.500
A place where no subway
could ever possibly go.

643
00:51:12.500 --> 00:51:14.400
Get it?

644
00:51:17.100 --> 00:51:19.600
Okay, you guys, listen...

645
00:51:19.700 --> 00:51:21.700
just because Kimberly
has these visions,

646
00:51:21.800 --> 00:51:23.400
it doesn't mean
we're not all capable

647
00:51:23.600 --> 00:51:25.300
of seeing signs
to some extent.

648
00:51:25.400 --> 00:51:27.000
Okay, okay, look.

649
00:51:27.100 --> 00:51:28.500
I gotta call bullshit.

650
00:51:28.500 --> 00:51:30.100
I mean, I've sat here
and listened

651
00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:32.200
to all your theories
and all your stories,

652
00:51:32.300 --> 00:51:34.200
and I think it's just
all bullshit.

653
00:51:34.300 --> 00:51:35.900
Call it what you want!

654
00:51:35.900 --> 00:51:38.600
- It'll keep your arse alive.
- Darlin', my arse is alive!

655
00:51:38.800 --> 00:51:40.600
Has been all day.

656
00:51:41.800 --> 00:51:44.000
There is nobody after us
but you,

657
00:51:44.100 --> 00:51:46.200
trying to make us all crazy.

658
00:51:59.800 --> 00:52:01.500
I should have seen that coming.

659
00:52:01.400 --> 00:52:02.900
Yeah.

660
00:52:03.100 --> 00:52:05.200
If Death is out to get you,

661
00:52:05.300 --> 00:52:07.300
why don't you get
the hell away from us?

662
00:52:07.400 --> 00:52:09.400
She's the only one that's
dealt with this before.

663
00:52:09.500 --> 00:52:11.500
We need to look out
for each other from now on.

664
00:52:11.500 --> 00:52:13.000
Sleep in shifts.

665
00:52:13.000 --> 00:52:15.300
We need to safe-proof
this death-trap.

666
00:52:24.400 --> 00:52:26.400
Get you to step out
of the van, miss?

667
00:52:26.500 --> 00:52:28.400
Are you kidding me?

668
00:52:28.600 --> 00:52:31.600
- What did I do?
- This vehicle's been reported stolen.

669
00:52:33.500 --> 00:52:35.500
Ohh!

670
00:52:35.700 --> 00:52:37.800
Screw this.
I'm going for a smoke.

671
00:52:37.900 --> 00:52:40.400
No, no, no,
it's not safe out there.

672
00:52:40.500 --> 00:52:43.000
So, Nora's got
to bite it before me anyhow, huh?

673
00:52:43.000 --> 00:52:45.800
Oh, you people have
no sense of humour.

674
00:52:52.300 --> 00:52:54.500
Nora, you okay?

675
00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:58.700
Four years ago
my husband died.

676
00:52:59.600 --> 00:53:01.700
Now Tim.
There's nothing left for me.

677
00:53:01.800 --> 00:53:03.600
Don't say that, okay?

678
00:53:03.800 --> 00:53:06.200
If it is my time to go
and be in heaven...

679
00:53:06.200 --> 00:53:08.700
with my family,
I can accept that.

680
00:53:08.800 --> 00:53:12.400
You got to trust me.
We can fight this.

681
00:53:12.600 --> 00:53:14.400
If we just stick
together long enough

682
00:53:14.400 --> 00:53:15.900
for her
to have her baby...

683
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:18.400
If you'll excuse me,
I have a funeral to plan.

684
00:53:19.600 --> 00:53:21.200
Nora.

685
00:53:23.900 --> 00:53:25.600
What do you think
you're doing?

686
00:53:25.600 --> 00:53:28.100
- I'm finished. I'm out.
- Don't leave, Eugene.

687
00:53:28.200 --> 00:53:30.000
Look, look.

688
00:53:30.100 --> 00:53:32.000
I control my life, alright?

689
00:53:32.100 --> 00:53:34.900
Not some crazy list that
Death has put together.

690
00:53:36.200 --> 00:53:38.300
I'll be sure to carve
that into your tombstone.

691
00:53:38.400 --> 00:53:40.800
Whatever. You may be able
to scare these people,

692
00:53:40.900 --> 00:53:43.200
- I'm not buying that shit.
- Be careful, man.

693
00:53:43.300 --> 00:53:44.800
- Hey.
- What?

694
00:53:44.800 --> 00:53:47.700
Even if you don't believe,
give this to Nora.

695
00:53:58.300 --> 00:54:00.100
I'm just going
to put this in the...

696
00:54:01.200 --> 00:54:02.800
closet.

697
00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:32.800
Sorry.

698
00:54:48.600 --> 00:54:50.400
Whoa.

699
00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:01.900
Man with hooks?

700
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:04.700
Man with hooks.

701
00:55:04.900 --> 00:55:07.200
Hey, I think I see
a man with hooks.

702
00:55:08.800 --> 00:55:10.300
Is that...

703
00:55:11.900 --> 00:55:13.700
- a sign?
- Oh my God.

704
00:55:13.700 --> 00:55:15.200
- Do you guys see that?
- He's right.

705
00:55:15.300 --> 00:55:16.700
- The phone.
- Shit.

706
00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:38.800
What the fuck?

707
00:55:48.900 --> 00:55:50.400
- Hello?
- Nora!

708
00:55:50.500 --> 00:55:53.300
- Who is this?
- Can you hear me?!

709
00:55:53.300 --> 00:55:55.900
Officer Burke,
I can't...

710
00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:57.600
I can't hear you!
What?!

711
00:55:57.700 --> 00:55:58.800
What does he...
What?!

712
00:55:58.900 --> 00:56:00.900
A man with hooks
is going to kill you.

713
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:02.400
- What, what?
- Oh...

714
00:56:02.500 --> 00:56:04.100
What is it, Nora?

715
00:56:06.600 --> 00:56:08.000
No!

716
00:56:08.100 --> 00:56:10.300
- Wait, wait!
- Let go!

717
00:56:10.300 --> 00:56:12.100
Wait, wait, Nora!

718
00:56:12.200 --> 00:56:14.100
- Get me out of here!
- Will you stop it?!

719
00:56:14.200 --> 00:56:15.500
Let me help!

720
00:56:15.600 --> 00:56:16.900
Let me go!

721
00:56:23.900 --> 00:56:26.100
Let go of me!

722
00:56:32.700 --> 00:56:34.500
Kat!

723
00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:47.100
Help me!

724
00:56:47.200 --> 00:56:49.600
- Wait!
- I don't want to die!

725
00:57:01.900 --> 00:57:03.800
Aah!
Let me out of here.

726
00:57:05.900 --> 00:57:07.800
I got it, thanks.
They found the van.

727
00:57:07.900 --> 00:57:10.700
Isabella's being held at
the Greenwood Lake sheriff's station.

728
00:57:10.700 --> 00:57:12.900
I'm in control of my life!

729
00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:15.100
- Kiss my arse!
- Eugene, what is it?

730
00:57:15.200 --> 00:57:17.100
- I control my life!
- What happened, Eugene?

731
00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:19.800
- You hear me, you Reaper cocksucker?!
- Calm down.

732
00:57:19.900 --> 00:57:22.100
- What happened? Where's Nora?
- Back the fuck up!

733
00:57:22.200 --> 00:57:24.900
- Whoa, whoa, okay!
- Back the fuck up!

734
00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:27.400
Eugene, what's wrong?
Just tell us what happened.

735
00:57:27.500 --> 00:57:29.400
Alright, give me
the gun, Eugene.

736
00:57:29.500 --> 00:57:31.600
- Give me the gun.
- No! Fuck no!

737
00:57:31.700 --> 00:57:34.700
Eugene, you just got
to relax, bro', okay?

738
00:57:34.700 --> 00:57:36.700
You just got
to calm down, man.

739
00:57:36.800 --> 00:57:38.500
Give me the gun.
Give me the gun, Eugene!

740
00:57:38.600 --> 00:57:41.400
- No, no, no, no!
- Don't do it! Don't do it!

741
00:57:41.500 --> 00:57:43.500
- I ain't going out like that.
- Hey, Eugene, no!

742
00:57:43.500 --> 00:57:46.100
- On my terms!
- Oh my God!

743
00:57:46.300 --> 00:57:48.000
You hear me!

744
00:57:48.100 --> 00:57:50.900
God!

745
00:57:59.400 --> 00:58:01.300
Oh!

746
00:58:01.400 --> 00:58:02.700
You don't keep it loaded?

747
00:58:04.100 --> 00:58:06.700
- Maybe they're all duds.
- Six in a row?

748
00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:09.900
Never.
That's impossible.

749
00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:12.100
It wasn't his turn to die.

750
00:58:13.600 --> 00:58:16.100
Can we find
the pregnant woman, now, please?

751
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:25.000
Is this safe, guys?

752
00:58:25.100 --> 00:58:27.400
I mean, someone in this car
is about to get whacked.

753
00:58:27.500 --> 00:58:29.900
Do the rest of us really feel
like sitting next to him?

754
00:58:29.900 --> 00:58:31.700
Or her?

755
00:58:33.000 --> 00:58:34.600
Hopefully her.

756
00:58:35.800 --> 00:58:37.600
Okay, guys,
let's not panic.

757
00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:40.200
- Isabella's safe.
- How do you know?

758
00:58:41.400 --> 00:58:43.500
You said she was going
to drive into a lake.

759
00:58:43.600 --> 00:58:46.300
How can she if she's
in protective custody?

760
00:58:53.600 --> 00:58:55.100
Look at me.

761
00:58:55.300 --> 00:58:57.200
Come on.

762
00:58:57.300 --> 00:58:59.200
Does it look like
I'm in the condition

763
00:58:59.300 --> 00:59:01.600
to commit grand theft auto?
This is insane.

764
00:59:01.700 --> 00:59:03.500
Look, hopefully
the district judge

765
00:59:03.600 --> 00:59:06.400
will have it all sorted out
by Monday morning, okay?

766
00:59:12.700 --> 00:59:14.600
Marcus.

767
00:59:14.600 --> 00:59:17.000
Marcus, Marcus.

768
00:59:17.100 --> 00:59:19.300
When I get out of here,
I am going to sue his...

769
00:59:21.300 --> 00:59:24.100
- Oh my God.
- What, what now?

770
00:59:24.100 --> 00:59:26.000
My water just broke.

771
00:59:26.100 --> 00:59:27.900
- What?
- My water, it just broke.

772
00:59:28.100 --> 00:59:30.700
- I'm gonna have my baby.
- No, not here.

773
00:59:30.700 --> 00:59:33.500
- No, you can't do this to me.
- Don't just stand there!

774
00:59:33.600 --> 00:59:36.500
- Get me to a hospital!
- Give me a second to think!

775
00:59:36.700 --> 00:59:39.800
I am not going to have my baby
in a jail cell!

776
00:59:39.900 --> 00:59:41.500
Get me to the hospital!

777
00:59:41.600 --> 00:59:43.400
Okay, okay!

778
00:59:43.500 --> 00:59:46.400
Sheriff Perry,
this is Deputy Adams, come back.

779
00:59:47.600 --> 00:59:50.000
God, I need the car!
Sheriff Perry, I need the car!

780
00:59:50.200 --> 00:59:52.300
My van! My van!
Take my van!

781
00:59:54.500 --> 00:59:56.000
Okay. Okay.

782
00:59:56.200 --> 00:59:58.200
Yeah, we'll go.
We'll go.

783
00:59:58.300 --> 01:00:00.200
Yeah, we'll go.

784
01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:05.300
Come on,
come on!

785
01:00:09.900 --> 01:00:12.300
Y'all want to hear
something crazy?

786
01:00:12.400 --> 01:00:14.400
It's not the first time
I cheated Death.

787
01:00:16.800 --> 01:00:19.700
A kid came to school
with a knife...

788
01:00:19.700 --> 01:00:21.500
killed his teacher.

789
01:00:23.200 --> 01:00:25.300
Teacher would have
been me,

790
01:00:25.300 --> 01:00:28.900
but I was transferred to another
school two days before.

791
01:00:28.900 --> 01:00:31.000
That's fucking weird, man.

792
01:00:31.100 --> 01:00:32.300
You want weird?

793
01:00:32.400 --> 01:00:34.400
Last year my partner and I
were heading out

794
01:00:34.400 --> 01:00:36.400
when a call came in
about a train wreck.

795
01:00:36.500 --> 01:00:38.600
Frank decided
to let me handle it alone.

796
01:00:40.700 --> 01:00:42.800
He died that night
in a shootout.

797
01:00:43.800 --> 01:00:46.800
If that call had come in
just 10 seconds later,

798
01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:48.700
I'd be dead, too.

799
01:00:48.700 --> 01:00:50.800
Oh my God.

800
01:00:50.800 --> 01:00:52.600
I'm sorry.

801
01:00:52.700 --> 01:00:54.200
It's just I got one, too.

802
01:00:54.400 --> 01:00:56.500
Okay, so last May
I'm supposed to go and stay

803
01:00:56.500 --> 01:00:59.100
at this cheesy little
bed and breakfast in Pennsylvania.

804
01:00:59.200 --> 01:01:02.000
Anyhow, there's this major gas leak
that no one knows about,

805
01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:04.300
and all the guests suffocated
during the night.

806
01:01:04.400 --> 01:01:05.600
So what happened?

807
01:01:05.800 --> 01:01:07.300
I don't know.
I never made it.

808
01:01:07.400 --> 01:01:10.000
The bus I was on splattered
some girl all over the road.

809
01:01:10.100 --> 01:01:11.400
Was that in Mt Abraham?

810
01:01:11.400 --> 01:01:14.700
Yes. How did you know?

811
01:01:14.900 --> 01:01:17.400
That bus you were on killed
Terry Chaney.

812
01:01:18.600 --> 01:01:20.800
She was supposed to die
on Flight 180.

813
01:01:23.800 --> 01:01:26.600
Hey, do you guys remember
that theatre in Paris

814
01:01:26.700 --> 01:01:29.300
that collapsed last year
and killed everybody inside?

815
01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:33.300
Well, I had tickets to go.

816
01:01:33.400 --> 01:01:35.700
But one night I'm in Paris

817
01:01:35.800 --> 01:01:38.900
and I'm just
tripping on acid

818
01:01:38.900 --> 01:01:41.000
and sipping lattes and such.

819
01:01:41.200 --> 01:01:43.000
And then all of a sudden

820
01:01:43.100 --> 01:01:46.100
this dude out of nowhere

821
01:01:46.100 --> 01:01:48.400
just gets whacked
by this falling sign.

822
01:01:48.500 --> 01:01:51.100
- Carter.
- Wait, wait, wait.

823
01:01:51.200 --> 01:01:53.700
The teacher I replaced,
her name was Val Lewton.

824
01:01:53.800 --> 01:01:56.600
She was from Mt Abraham.
She died in an explosion.

825
01:01:56.700 --> 01:01:59.500
Shit. The call about
the train wreck

826
01:01:59.600 --> 01:02:01.100
that saved my life...

827
01:02:01.100 --> 01:02:03.400
that was the night
I scraped up Billy Hitchcock.

828
01:02:03.600 --> 01:02:06.000
Wait a minute.
Who are these people?

829
01:02:07.300 --> 01:02:09.200
The people who got off
of Flight 180.

830
01:02:10.900 --> 01:02:13.000
They were my friends.

831
01:02:16.200 --> 01:02:18.400
Kimberly,
tell us what happened.

832
01:02:21.500 --> 01:02:24.500
About a year ago my mum and I
were at the mall.

833
01:02:24.700 --> 01:02:26.500
I was supposed
to meet her outside,

834
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:28.900
but I got caught up watching
this news report

835
01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:30.800
about some kid
that committed suicide.

836
01:02:32.300 --> 01:02:34.000
I kept thinking,

837
01:02:34.100 --> 01:02:36.400
'How can you strangle yourself
in the bathtub?

838
01:02:36.500 --> 01:02:38.200
That's stupid.'

839
01:02:40.700 --> 01:02:42.600
It felt wrong.

840
01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.400
And yet...

841
01:02:47.200 --> 01:02:50.400
I heard some gunshots
and I ran outside.

842
01:02:52.400 --> 01:02:54.900
Some kids were trying
to steal my mum's car.

843
01:02:55.100 --> 01:02:57.500
She tried to fight them off,
she was a fighter,

844
01:02:57.600 --> 01:02:59.600
and they killed her.

845
01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:04.500
After the funeral I kept thinking that
it should have been me.

846
01:03:06.100 --> 01:03:07.900
I guess everyone must
think that.

847
01:03:09.500 --> 01:03:11.500
But I guess I was right.

848
01:03:20.200 --> 01:03:23.100
Get there.
Could you drive a little faster maybe?!

849
01:03:23.300 --> 01:03:25.000
- I'm going as fast as I can.
- God!

850
01:03:27.000 --> 01:03:29.000
When we got off
Flight 180,

851
01:03:29.100 --> 01:03:31.900
it didn't just change
our lives.

852
01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:34.300
It affected everyone
and everything

853
01:03:34.400 --> 01:03:36.500
we've come
into contact with since.

854
01:03:36.600 --> 01:03:38.500
I'm not sure
I'm understanding you.

855
01:03:38.600 --> 01:03:40.900
Being alive after
we were supposed to die,

856
01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:42.900
it caused an outward ripple.

857
01:03:43.000 --> 01:03:44.800
A rift in Death's design.

858
01:03:44.900 --> 01:03:47.800
So if you had never
gotten off the plane...

859
01:03:49.300 --> 01:03:51.400
we wouldn't be alive
in the first place.

860
01:03:51.500 --> 01:03:53.900
Yes, that's why Death
is working backwards!

861
01:03:54.000 --> 01:03:56.000
It's tying up
all the loose ends,

862
01:03:56.100 --> 01:03:58.300
Sealing the rift once
and for all.

863
01:04:19.400 --> 01:04:20.700
Oh, shit!

864
01:04:22.600 --> 01:04:24.200
Jesus Christ!

865
01:04:26.800 --> 01:04:28.700
Hang on! Hang on!

866
01:04:47.900 --> 01:04:50.100
- Is everybody alright?
- Oh God.

867
01:04:52.400 --> 01:04:54.000
God, Eugene!

868
01:04:54.100 --> 01:04:57.100
- He can't breathe.
- Oh, my legs!

869
01:04:59.900 --> 01:05:01.500
No, please.

870
01:05:01.700 --> 01:05:04.300
- It's not going to wait.
- I got to go help those people.

871
01:05:04.300 --> 01:05:06.400
Do you want to deliver
this baby?

872
01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:10.700
Those people can help.
Let's go.

873
01:05:12.200 --> 01:05:14.500
Officer Adams reporting
a vehicle collision

874
01:05:14.600 --> 01:05:16.600
off 9-A
at the 180 mile-marker.

875
01:05:16.700 --> 01:05:18.400
Send all emergency vehicles
to the scene.

876
01:05:18.500 --> 01:05:21.400
- We have to go. Go!
- Okay, okay, okay!

877
01:05:21.500 --> 01:05:24.100
Just... okay, okay!
We're going! We're going!

878
01:05:25.800 --> 01:05:28.600
- Easy, easy.
- Here, here, here.

879
01:05:28.600 --> 01:05:30.800
I think he has
a collapsed lung.

880
01:05:30.800 --> 01:05:33.300
- Everyone okay?
- Call an ambulance!

881
01:05:38.200 --> 01:05:40.400
Stay with us.

882
01:05:40.500 --> 01:05:41.800
Hey, hey you!

883
01:05:41.900 --> 01:05:45.700
Hey! Come on.
Help me out.

884
01:05:45.800 --> 01:05:49.200
You got to get me out of here before
this thing explodes or something, okay?

885
01:05:51.900 --> 01:05:53.400
I think it's okay.

886
01:05:53.400 --> 01:05:55.600
I don't smell any gas
and nothing's dripping.

887
01:05:55.700 --> 01:05:58.400
Alright, get this thing off me.
Just pull. Hurry.

888
01:05:58.400 --> 01:06:00.500
Okay. Be careful.
Ready?

889
01:06:01.900 --> 01:06:04.800
Oh God, Jethro!
Jesus Christ!

890
01:06:04.800 --> 01:06:07.000
I got to be able to use
my legs when I'm done.

891
01:06:07.100 --> 01:06:09.100
I'm so... Dad!

892
01:06:15.000 --> 01:06:16.600
Eugene, everything's
going to be okay.

893
01:06:16.600 --> 01:06:19.300
If he doesn't get a respirator,
he's not going to make it!

894
01:06:19.400 --> 01:06:22.200
We're going to get you to the hospital.
Be careful with that!

895
01:06:22.200 --> 01:06:25.500
Check the gauges on the regulator,
and watch out for overdoses!

896
01:06:25.600 --> 01:06:28.600
- And look out for potholes and puddles.
- You can't come in, miss.

897
01:06:30.200 --> 01:06:32.300
And watch out
for power lines!

898
01:06:33.700 --> 01:06:35.600
Watch it!

899
01:06:40.900 --> 01:06:43.300
You trying to get yourself killed,
little boy?

900
01:06:43.400 --> 01:06:45.600
You got to use
your head, man.

901
01:06:45.600 --> 01:06:47.300
Get that news van back.

902
01:06:47.400 --> 01:06:48.900
Thanks.

903
01:06:56.300 --> 01:06:57.900
Okay, let's go.

904
01:07:13.500 --> 01:07:15.800
How is she doing?

905
01:07:15.900 --> 01:07:17.900
I think she's going
to be okay.

906
01:07:20.600 --> 01:07:23.200
- Can I ask you a question?
- Yeah.

907
01:07:25.100 --> 01:07:27.000
When I die...

908
01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:28.800
is it going to hurt?

909
01:07:30.200 --> 01:07:31.900
I don't know.

910
01:07:33.300 --> 01:07:35.000
You're going to die after me, right?

911
01:07:36.300 --> 01:07:38.000
Yeah, I guess so.

912
01:07:40.000 --> 01:07:41.900
Would you take these?

913
01:07:47.400 --> 01:07:49.200
And if I die...

914
01:07:51.900 --> 01:07:53.600
would you throw out
all my drugs

915
01:07:53.800 --> 01:07:57.500
and my paraphernalia
and my porno?

916
01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:01.400
You know...

917
01:08:01.300 --> 01:08:03.700
anything that's going
to break my mum's heart.

918
01:08:04.900 --> 01:08:06.600
Please?

919
01:08:09.800 --> 01:08:11.400
Thank you.

920
01:08:15.500 --> 01:08:17.200
This is Cheyenne Jacobson

921
01:08:17.400 --> 01:08:19.200
reporting live
from the Gibbons farm.

922
01:08:19.300 --> 01:08:20.900
Sheriff Perry,
Officer Burke here.

923
01:08:21.000 --> 01:08:23.500
I'm trying to get some
information on Isabella...

924
01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:25.400
She did?

925
01:08:25.500 --> 01:08:28.000
Okay. Thanks.
Great.

926
01:08:28.100 --> 01:08:29.500
Kimberly!

927
01:08:29.500 --> 01:08:32.000
Isabella's at Lakeview Hospital.
They're prepping her for delivery.

928
01:08:32.200 --> 01:08:34.000
- We got to go now.
- What about Kat?

929
01:08:34.000 --> 01:08:35.200
I'll go talk to her.

930
01:08:35.400 --> 01:08:38.100
Hi.

931
01:08:38.200 --> 01:08:40.600
Just find Isabella and get this thing
over with, okay?

932
01:08:40.700 --> 01:08:42.300
Go on, I'll be fine.

933
01:08:49.000 --> 01:08:50.900
- Where's Rory?
- I don't know.

934
01:08:54.800 --> 01:08:57.500
Could you be a little quieter
with that thing, please?

935
01:08:57.500 --> 01:09:00.300
Yeah, sure.
I'll just put it on quiet mode.

936
01:09:00.500 --> 01:09:01.800
That would be good.

937
01:09:28.800 --> 01:09:29.900
Rory.

938
01:09:45.300 --> 01:09:47.500
Oh my God!

939
01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:49.500
Somebody get out there!

940
01:09:49.600 --> 01:09:52.400
- We have to get to the hospital now!
- Well, take my truck!

941
01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:53.900
The keys are in it.

942
01:09:57.600 --> 01:09:59.800
Kimberly!

943
01:10:10.500 --> 01:10:11.800
Kimberly!

944
01:10:11.800 --> 01:10:13.900
- Kimberly.
- What do you see?

945
01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:16.400
- What are we looking for?
- It's not here.

946
01:10:18.200 --> 01:10:20.000
This one was different.

947
01:10:20.100 --> 01:10:23.000
It was like the van crashing
into the lake.

948
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:25.000
I was in a hospital,
there was screaming

949
01:10:25.100 --> 01:10:26.700
and a nurse was trying
to choke me.

950
01:10:26.800 --> 01:10:29.300
I couldn't see her,
but I could see her name tag.

951
01:10:29.400 --> 01:10:31.200
It was right in my face.
Kalarjian.

952
01:10:32.800 --> 01:10:35.800
I think a nurse named
Kalarjian is going to try and kill Isabella.

953
01:10:39.700 --> 01:10:42.500
Listen to me, Isabella!
I need you to stop pushing!

954
01:10:42.600 --> 01:10:44.000
What's wrong?
Is my baby alright?

955
01:10:44.200 --> 01:10:46.500
The cord's around the neck.
This baby's in trouble.

956
01:10:46.600 --> 01:10:49.300
A bizarre accident
has left two people dead,

957
01:10:49.300 --> 01:10:52.000
one of them killed
by a safety device meant to protect us.

958
01:10:52.100 --> 01:10:54.500
Ironically, the woman
was impaled through the head

959
01:10:54.500 --> 01:10:56.800
after her emergency airbag
deployed.

960
01:10:56.900 --> 01:11:00.300
She was trapped in her vehicle after it
crashed into a field near Greenwood Lake.

961
01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:02.800
Suddenly the airbag went off...

962
01:11:35.700 --> 01:11:37.700
Isabella Hudson!
What room is she in?

963
01:11:37.900 --> 01:11:39.900
We may need to do
a stat Caesarean!

964
01:11:40.000 --> 01:11:41.700
Get Dr Kalarjian
up here now!

965
01:11:41.800 --> 01:11:44.400
Dr Kalarjian, code blue.
Delivery room six.

966
01:11:44.500 --> 01:11:45.800
I'm just going
to wait outside,

967
01:11:45.800 --> 01:11:47.700
'cause I'm just really
in the way here.

968
01:11:47.800 --> 01:11:49.600
- Don't you dare leave me!
- Okay, okay.

969
01:11:49.700 --> 01:11:51.400
You guys, get to Isabella!

970
01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:53.300
I'm going to find Eugene!

971
01:11:53.400 --> 01:11:56.400
Dr Kalarjian, code blue.
Delivery room six.

972
01:11:56.500 --> 01:11:59.300
Dr Kalarjian, delivery room six.
Code blue.

973
01:12:14.300 --> 01:12:16.500
Dr Kalarjian,
in here, hurry!

974
01:12:17.600 --> 01:12:19.700
That's her.

975
01:12:20.700 --> 01:12:22.200
Wait, wait, wait!

976
01:12:57.900 --> 01:13:00.100
Contractions have stopped.

977
01:13:00.200 --> 01:13:02.600
Arrest in descent halfway
through the birth canal.

978
01:13:02.700 --> 01:13:04.700
Bad tracing,
it's losing oxygen.

979
01:13:04.800 --> 01:13:06.800
The cord's compressed!

980
01:13:06.900 --> 01:13:10.000
- Down to 40.
- Oh God! What's happening?!

981
01:13:10.100 --> 01:13:11.700
Where's Kalarjian?!

982
01:13:11.800 --> 01:13:14.400
Dr Kalarjian!

983
01:13:14.500 --> 01:13:16.500
- Dr Kalarjian!
- Not now, I'm busy.

984
01:13:16.600 --> 01:13:19.700
- Ow! Hey! Hey!
- Police business.

985
01:13:28.600 --> 01:13:31.000
Just push a little more.

986
01:13:31.100 --> 01:13:33.400
Oh, no.

987
01:13:33.500 --> 01:13:35.100
Isabella, is the baby okay?

988
01:13:36.400 --> 01:13:37.900
I'm sorry.
You can't be here.

989
01:13:37.900 --> 01:13:40.400
- I have to ask you to leave.
- I need to know...

990
01:13:40.500 --> 01:13:43.200
I need to know if the baby's alright!

991
01:13:44.700 --> 01:13:46.500
It's a boy.

992
01:14:06.400 --> 01:14:08.300
Thank you.
Congratulations!

993
01:14:08.400 --> 01:14:10.300
Who the hell are they?

994
01:14:10.300 --> 01:14:12.600
Oh my God!

995
01:14:16.300 --> 01:14:18.000
- Clear.
- I can't find Eugene.

996
01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:20.600
- No, don't worry. She had the baby!
- It's okay.

997
01:14:20.700 --> 01:14:22.600
It's over.
It's okay.

998
01:14:35.500 --> 01:14:37.800
- Kimberly.
- What did you see?

999
01:14:37.900 --> 01:14:41.100
I don't think Isabella
was ever supposed to die in that pileup.

1000
01:14:41.200 --> 01:14:43.400
Then what's the premonition
of the lake supposed to mean?

1001
01:14:43.500 --> 01:14:45.200
Try to remember.

1002
01:15:01.900 --> 01:15:05.000
Bloody hands.
Someone with bloody hands.

1003
01:15:06.100 --> 01:15:07.400
Eugene.

1004
01:15:11.700 --> 01:15:14.700
Only new life defeats death.
What is that supposed to mean?

1005
01:15:14.800 --> 01:15:16.600
You saw an ECG machine
and what else?

1006
01:15:18.400 --> 01:15:20.400
Bloody hands.
What else did you see, Kimberly?

1007
01:15:21.500 --> 01:15:22.900
Wait.

1008
01:15:24.700 --> 01:15:26.500
Eugene.

1009
01:15:45.800 --> 01:15:47.600
Oh God, no!

1010
01:15:57.500 --> 01:15:59.100
Bloody hands.

1011
01:16:00.900 --> 01:16:02.900
It's me.
The premonitions are about me.

1012
01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:05.000
- What?
- Crash cart.

1013
01:16:05.100 --> 01:16:06.500
Let's go! Move it!

1014
01:16:08.700 --> 01:16:10.500
Dr Kalarjian.

1015
01:16:10.600 --> 01:16:12.300
ECG machine.

1016
01:16:16.700 --> 01:16:18.200
The lake.

1017
01:16:18.300 --> 01:16:20.100
The white van.

1018
01:16:24.700 --> 01:16:26.400
What are you talking about?

1019
01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:30.800
New life.

1020
